# Where the game server is, for production builds only.
#
# Committed rather than set as a dashboard variable, because it is not a
# secret: it is a URL that ships inside the page's JavaScript, readable by
# anyone who opens the game. Keeping it here means a clean checkout builds a
# working site, and that the thing production depends on is reviewable in a
# diff rather than invisible in somebody's browser tab.
#
# Only `astro build` reads this. `npm run dev` deliberately does not, so a
# local checkout keeps falling back to the same-browser transport where two
# tabs play each other - which is how the protocol was debugged and how it
# should stay debuggable. To point local dev at a server anyway:
#
#   PUBLIC_DEADBALL_ROOMS=http://127.0.0.1:8787 npm run dev
#
# See workers/deadball/README.md.
PUBLIC_DEADBALL_ROOMS=https://deadball-rooms.phil-4a3.workers.dev
